				(property "Description" "Pololu D36V50F5 (item #4091) step-down: 5V out, 5.5A typical at 36V in, input 5.5-50V, 1in square, 12-pin 2x6 header on 0.1in grid, three M2 mounting holes. As-built pin layout by column (row1/row2): col1 VOUT/VOUT, col2 GND/GND, col3 GND/GND, col4 VIN/VIN, col5 VRP/VRP, col6 EN/PG. Four GND pins and doubled VOUT/VIN/VRP carry the current; EN and PG are the only single pins. VRP is reverse-protected VIN. Powers the logic domain from the M18 electronics pack (~21V). NOTE: col6 assumes row 1 = the odd-pad row, so pad 11 = EN and pad 12 = PG; if the rows run the other way those two swap."
					(at 0 0 0)
					(show_name no)
					(do_not_autoplace no)
					(hide yes)
					(effects
						(font
							(size 1.27 1.27)
